# System Map

## Purpose
Describe the system's users, core outcomes, and scope in a few sentences.

## Key Concepts
Define stable project terms, distinctions, and avoided synonyms when they help explain the system.

## Use-Case Catalog
List known use cases by actor and outcome, marking current, next, or later horizon.

## Responsibilities
Name only meaningful components or modules and state what each owns. Follow applicable project instructions for organization.

## Relationships and Dependencies
Describe relevant relationships, dependency direction, data ownership, integration points, and important external systems.

## Public Contracts
List stable APIs, commands, events, schemas, error semantics, and compatibility commitments.

## Constraints
Record technical, operational, security, regulatory, performance, and consistency constraints that shape changes.

## Extension Pressures and Risks
Record known variation, likely growth points, costly retrofits, fragile boundaries, and material unknowns without prebuilding solutions.
